Window out of sight = app in the background; Android notifications in the macOS Notification Center

Lifecycle: a window nobody can see (minimized, Cmd+H, fully covered, displays asleep) puts the top activity through onPause/onStop after a 1 s grace, and back through onRestart/onStart/onResume when it shows again (ActivityHost.macapkWindowVisibility, the hostCover pair). While the guest is in the background the host present idles at MACAPK_HIDDEN_DRIVE_HZ even when MACAPK_PAUSE_WHEN_HIDDEN=0. MACAPK_BACKGROUND_WHEN_HIDDEN=0 turns it off; MACAPK_BACKGROUND_ON_OCCLUSION=0 leaves covered windows out. Measured on Instagram: CPU 21% visible -> 9-14% minimized; Instagram logs "Moving to background", releases its players and recreates them on return (video and sound back).

Notifications: NotificationManager.notify/cancel go to host_notifications.mm, which posts through a bundled helper app (Contents/Helpers/InstamacNotifier.app, tools/notifier in the Instamac repo) by distributed notification; a click brings the window back and fires the contentIntent. Skips ongoing, progress, group-summary and muted-channel notifications and anything while the app is in front. Dock badge = posted and not cancelled. MACAPK_NOTIFY_SELFTEST=1 posts one on going to the background; injector verbs miniaturize/deminiaturize/hide/unhide drive the window without input.

